            <ArticleTitle>Dissecting intramural hematoma in esophageal carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>221-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 50-year-old man with esophageal carcinoma developed severe, refractory, retrosternal chest pain. The diagnosis was made four days later when contrast studies showed an intramural dissecting hematoma of the esophagus. The patient responded to conservative management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
